{# OAuth 2.0 Form Post Response Mode §2: the answer of the authorization endpoint handed to the user agent
   as a form it posts to the redirect URI, so that no parameter of the answer is ever written in a URL.
   This page does not extend the layout of the interaction plane, on purpose: it carries a response of the
   protocol rather than a page of the product, and its Content-Security-Policy is "default-src 'none'" with
   the one script below named by its hash, which a layout bringing a stylesheet or a script of its own
   would break. A browser that runs the script never reads a word of it; the sentence and the button are
   what a browser without scripting shows. Whoever edits it keeps the script exactly as it is given: its
   hash is the policy. #}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale|replace({'_': '-'}) }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{ 'form_post.title'|trans }}</title>
</head>
<body>
    <main>
        <p>{{ 'form_post.explanation'|trans }}</p>
        <form method="post" action="{{ redirect_uri }}">
            {% for name, value in parameters %}
                <input type="hidden" name="{{ name }}" value="{{ value }}">
            {% endfor %}
            <button type="submit">{{ 'form_post.continue'|trans }}</button>
        </form>
    </main>
    <script>{{ script|raw }}</script>
</body>
</html>
